messages.text:
@Alice @Bob — still in standup, one more before 10:00.

Feasibility settles this for me. Bob, 16:00–16:30 is your only window today, and Carol's out from 16:00 (dentist at 16:15, six weeks booked, can't move) — so the original split leaves T1 with no first meeting today, which the kickoff rules require. It doesn't give my pair a clean slot either: Alice, 15:00–15:30 clashes with a customer call I'm on 15:00–16:00, so we'd be down to 10:00–10:30, right as the board locks. The flip is the only split where both tickets are staffed and both kickoffs happen today: Carol + me at 14:30 (she's accepted), you two at 16:00–16:30.

On the merits: Alice, "each continues her own piece" argues against you here, not for you — the piece of T2 that's yours is the sign-off this review is examining. As the PM on T2 I'd rather the review came with the other pair of eyes. Bob, the cold-start point is the strongest thing the original split has going for it, but Carol's offered a direct handover, and the DS half of T1 is the eval harness — shared work, by both your accounts.

@Alice — please switch your claim to T1 before 10:00. Three of us on T2 leaves the board invalid, and the flip is the only configuration that satisfies the rules as pinned.

@Alice — credit where it's due first: you won the independence point, and Carol's conceded it — so do I. "The other pair of eyes" overreached; I withdraw it. And you're right that the claims are the time-critical thing, not the meetings — which is exactly why the switch is the only move left before 10:00.

On feasibility, you set the test yourself: "if there is truly nothing in six hours you can move, say so and I'll treat the feasibility point as real." Bob has said so, with specifics — external vendor call, on-call handover, migration cutover, standup till 10:00; commitments with other parties attached, none movable before the lock. By your own criterion the point is real: under the original split, T1's pair has no slot today at all. And the cold-start argument — the backbone of the original split — has been withdrawn by the person carrying T1, with a direct handover on the table.

So it's 3 of 4 for the flip, and the board stays invalid until your claim moves. If it locks as it stands, T1 runs without a data scientist and the sprint starts broken — the one outcome worse for your case than the flip. Please switch your claim to T1 before 10:00. Then the board's complete, you can report the assignments to Kira, and T1 is well set up: Carol's cold-start handover at 15:00–15:30, kickoff with Bob at 16:00–16:30.
